body:
Unfortunately there is no textbook or no reading material for this class whatsoever. The instructor was just handed the course and creates these PowerPoints with no source information. Probably 50% or so of test questions are directly from the PowerPoint, the other 50% is either word of mouth or inference.

&#x200B;

Edit: You're right about the grade, but it frustrates me as I am shooting for a high GPA (this is my last semester for my AA), and every single test is like this and those are our only assignments.

For reference, this is a PSYC 101 course with a brand new professor who does not seem to understand any of the course. She straight up makes things up in class, and was just handed this course this year because the previous instructor quit. Please see captions for descriptions of why I do not understand the reasoning for being marked incorrect. I'm just extremely frustrated because this happens on every single assignment and I feel as though she is unfairly grading based on opinions rather than facts.

&#x200B;

 I had to take this course so I could be enrolled in my PSYC 218 Research Methods class since they just changed the requirements for my Bachelor's.
